{"id": "EUVD-2026-45831", "enisaUuid": "59715b51-88b9-39b8-aa60-9bc2caed54f9", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nerofs: fix metabuf leak in inode xattr initialization\n\ncommit bb88e8da0025 (\"erofs: use meta buffers for xattr operations\")\nconverted xattr operations to use on-stack erofs_buf instances.\nerofs_init_inode_xattrs() uses such a metabuf while reading the inline\nxattr header and shared xattr id array.\n\nSome error paths after erofs_read_metabuf() leave through out_unlock\nwithout dropping the metabuf, so the folio reference can leak.\n\nConsolidate the cleanup at out_unlock. erofs_put_metabuf() is a\nno-op if no folio has been acquired, and this keeps all paths after\ntaking EROFS_I_BL_XATTR_BIT covered by a single cleanup site.", "datePublished": "2026-07-19T15:40:37", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:43:06", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3812cfe6cb0a5988df4fedcdaf9aab677b9cca61", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e4a552e0b6413c1af2e140b5bc14bb849b411b57", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fcb23bb31508b62e8a1b32adf6217820e90e29b0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/492c73b21fefa36f3869cb2b188ffb7fe37b3a9b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/79b09c54c6563df9846ca3094bcfd72082c3e1d7"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-64146", "GHSA-556c-3r39-wvfx"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "25760bd9-d3e4-3ccb-9e89-e74ae17c3216", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "35841555-3a9f-32bf-8196-837b14ed043f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bb88e8da00253bea0e7f0f4cdfd7910572d7799f <e4a552e0b6413c1af2e140b5bc14bb849b411b57"}, {"id": "4262d2ae-6e79-3e0c-9d90-31d0a25680aa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.17"}, {"id": "78a1384d-3ad9-39a4-b9f5-b5acbd4f172a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "a132bd76-f2a1-3cb1-9cd5-a6ac0e97ecc9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bb88e8da00253bea0e7f0f4cdfd7910572d7799f <492c73b21fefa36f3869cb2b188ffb7fe37b3a9b"}, {"id": "ad3bc908-8487-34c0-8fed-67f4e2c65308", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bb88e8da00253bea0e7f0f4cdfd7910572d7799f <3812cfe6cb0a5988df4fedcdaf9aab677b9cca61"}, {"id": "afd8d444-ca7e-374f-bb78-38e9ee09a8d9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bb88e8da00253bea0e7f0f4cdfd7910572d7799f <79b09c54c6563df9846ca3094bcfd72082c3e1d7"}, {"id": "d6d991ad-f539-3b60-b136-030d8e139ba6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0.11"}, {"id": "dcfd5ab5-2593-36f2-9c71-0e3dc189c93f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "de010c0c-2ddc-350a-abea-d0aef438bd6f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1"}, {"id": "deff1d9a-8b84-3545-9b54-31d204d72771", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "f17a73b6-2f8e-3a5e-bcdb-fe5cdd46b5f0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bb88e8da00253bea0e7f0f4cdfd7910572d7799f <fcb23bb31508b62e8a1b32adf6217820e90e29b0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "fc16a5fc-e6a4-3fe9-a2b1-2bde2bf15280", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}